msgctxt "#30270"
msgid "Seconds to wait for the Torrest daemon to answer after it starts (with Kodi, after a settings change or a crash). Torrent lists opened meanwhile wait as long. Raise it if the daemon is slow to start here (many torrents to restore, a slow device) and the log says \"Timed out waiting for daemon\"; lower it to give up sooner when it can't start."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30271"
msgid "Seconds a play waits for pre-buffering (Buffer start and Buffer end) before it gives up. Raise it for slow or poorly seeded torrents that would get there with more time; lower it to fail sooner on dead ones. 0 also means no limit."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30272"
msgid "Seconds a play (or a file download) waits for a magnet's metadata, its file list fetched from peers, before it gives up. Raise it for rare magnets with few peers; lower it to fail sooner on dead ones. 0 also means no limit."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30273"
msgid "Daemon setting: seconds a read from the stream waits for a missing piece before it fails. Raise it if a slow torrent's playback stops with read errors; lower it so a stalled stream fails sooner instead of hanging. 0 also means no limit."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30274"
msgid "Daemon setting: seconds a piece that is no longer read stays in memory. Higher keeps more in memory, so seeking back is quicker but uses more memory; lower frees memory sooner. It isn't a timeout that fails anything, so it can't be turned off."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30275"
msgid "Give up a play when buffering takes longer than the time below. Off: buffering goes on until it completes or you cancel it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30276"
msgid "Give up a play when a magnet's metadata takes longer than the time below to arrive. Off: it waits until the metadata arrives or you cancel it."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30277"
msgid "Let the daemon give up on a missing piece after the time below. Off: a read waits until the piece arrives, which can leave the player hanging on a stalled torrent."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30278"
msgid "Pause when the download falls behind"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30279"
msgid "Resume once ahead by (seconds)"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30280"
msgid "While a video plays, Torrest fetches the part just ahead of it first. When less than a few seconds of it are downloaded, the video pauses rather than running into the missing part (which can stop the player), and carries on by itself once the time below is ready. Off: playback runs on and may stall or stop on a slow torrent."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30281"
msgid "Seconds of video that must be downloaded past the play position before a paused video carries on. Higher pauses less often but for longer; lower carries on sooner but may pause again soon on a slow torrent."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30282"
msgid "Keep packs"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30283"
msgid "A torrent with more than one video (a season pack) is never deleted when playback stops, so one episode can't take the others with it. Off: the action above deletes the whole pack too."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30284"
msgid "Delete watched episodes from packs"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30285"
msgid "An episode watched to the end in a pack has its own file deleted; the rest of the pack is kept. The torrent is then added again, which checks what is on disk (this takes a while for a big pack): a piece the episode shared with its neighbours downloads again when they play. Off: a pack is always kept whole."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "#30286"
msgid "Do you want to delete this episode's file? The rest of the pack is kept."
msgstr ""

